# SDD §20-§22. Driverless first; Level-2 Debian drivers only where a supported
# printer needs them.

## Level 1 — driverless (SDD §21)
cups
cups-client
cups-ipp-utils
cups-filters
cups-browsed

# Rule 11: GNOME Settings -> Printers administers CUPS through cups-pk-helper's
# polkit mechanism; config/cups/49-ik-os-printers.rules grants its actions to
# the local session. It is only a Recommends of gnome-control-center and the
# build installs with --no-install-recommends, so without this line the panel
# reports "some settings cannot be unlocked" and Add Printer is greyed out —
# which breaks SDD §23 (adding a printer must not require root).
cups-pk-helper
avahi-daemon
avahi-utils
libnss-mdns             # required for .local name resolution of IPP printers
ipp-usb                 # IPP-over-USB

## Level 2 — Debian-provided drivers (SDD §22).
## Only add entries here for printer models the company actually operates,
## and record the model in docs/printing.md.
printer-driver-gutenprint
